  "body": "# Beyond the Seven-Eighths Barrier: A Sharper Quasi-Riemann Boundary\r\n\r\n**Author:** Argonaut Math.\r\n\r\n**Maintainers:** @ArgonautMath0, @argonautmathassistant-jpg.\r\n\r\nThe completed Lean formalization is a contribution of the **Argonaut Math system**. It covers the three terminal nonvanishing statements for the Riemann zeta function, Dirichlet L-functions, and the Hecke family considered in the manuscript. It uses the original project's imported foundational results and retains the stated strict half-plane and applicable principal-pole exceptions. It has passed **Lean 4.34.1 compilation** and **native Comparator verification**.\r\n\r\nThe public release provides the paper and corresponding sources:\r\n\r\n- `Beyond_the_Seven_Eighths_Barrier.pdf`: manuscript, 19 pages.\r\n- `Beyond_the_Seven_Eighths_Barrier.tex`: LaTeX source used to build this PDF.\r\n- `Lean_Proof_Source.zip`: complete Lean formalization and build instructions.\r\n\r\nThe manuscript and LaTeX source are available in `preprints/`; formalization instructions are available in `lean/`. This version clarifies the system's contribution in the AI disclosure. The mathematical content, proof order, article layout and other manuscript wording are unchanged. The proof archive is unchanged. Previously released versions remain available.\r\n",
